        },
        {
          "id": "p4-10",
          "speaker": "",
          "text": "And if you think about it, that’s quite sensible for a bird living in the city. Jonathan Atwell, in Indiana University, is looking at how a range of animals respond to urban environments."
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-11",
          "speaker": "",
          "text": "He’s found that when they’re under stress, their endocrine systems react by reducing the amount of hormones such as corticosterone into their blood. It’s a sensible-seeming adaptation."
        },
